WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.880
A rat cannot say a touch hurts.

2
00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:06.920
How do scientists measure pain, fear, or choice without words?

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:13.700
They use behavioural assays: standard tests that turn an animal's actions into a

4
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:14.780
measurable stand-in.

5
00:00:15.783 --> 00:00:17.303
Start with touch and pain.

6
00:00:19.023 --> 00:00:23.303
Researchers press calibrated filaments of increasing stiffness, called von Frey

7
00:00:23.303 --> 00:00:24.963
filaments, against a paw.

8
00:00:26.323 --> 00:00:31.163
Repeating the test estimates the withdrawal threshold, the force that makes the paw

9
00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:35.703
lift. Many labs use the force that lifts it half the time.

10
00:00:36.863 --> 00:00:41.743
A fall in that threshold is the rodent sign of allodynia, pain from a normally

11
00:00:41.743 --> 00:00:42.743
harmless touch.

12
00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:46.607
Assays also measure learning through conditioning.

13
00:00:48.027 --> 00:00:53.447
In Pavlovian threat conditioning, a harmless conditioned stimulus, like a tone, is

14
00:00:53.447 --> 00:00:54.827
paired with a brief footshock.

15
00:00:56.187 --> 00:01:01.087
That shock is an unconditioned stimulus because it causes an unlearned reaction.

16
00:01:02.487 --> 00:01:07.627
Later, the tone alone triggers conditioned responses: freezing still except for

17
00:01:07.627 --> 00:01:09.967
breathing, and rising arterial pressure.

18
00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:16.540
Here is the core rule: an assay measures an action, and paired controls separate its

19
00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:19.220
causes. Test that idea.

20
00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:25.820
Suppose you damage, or lesion, one target below the central amygdala, then condition

21
00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:31.840
rats to a tone. If that target drives only arterial pressure, what happens to

22
00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:32.840
freezing?

23
00:01:37.783 --> 00:01:41.083
Freezing stays intact while the pressure rise drops.

24
00:01:42.423 --> 00:01:46.623
Measuring two responses in the same animal guards against a blunt defect.

25
00:01:48.023 --> 00:01:51.903
If freezing survives, the lesion did not block threat learning itself.

26
00:01:53.283 --> 00:01:58.403
Still, readouts have strict limits: a paw lift measures a reflex, not a report of

27
00:01:58.403 --> 00:01:59.403
pain.

28
00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:03.567
Behaviour alone cannot tell which circuit mechanism changed.

29
00:02:04.727 --> 00:02:07.327
So scientists pair assays with neural tests.

30
00:02:08.967 --> 00:02:10.187
Recording tracks active cells.

31
00:02:11.547 --> 00:02:15.667
Stimulation tests whether they are enough, and silencing tests whether they are

32
00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:21.567
needed. A lifelong mutant is not an acute change, so when the loss happened matters.

33
00:02:23.027 --> 00:02:26.207
Conditions matter too: male and female mice can differ.

34
00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.520
Those controls let assays unlock major findings.

35
00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:37.400
In 1988, LeDoux, Iwata, Cicchetti and Reis tested threat conditioning in rats.

36
00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:43.420
Lateral-hypothalamic lesions impaired the pressure rise while sparing freezing.

37
00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:50.280
Lesions in a midbrain region, the caudal periaqueductal gray, disrupted freezing

38
00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:51.400
while sparing pressure.

39
00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:56.060
Measuring both responses separated two output routes.

40
00:02:57.033 --> 00:03:01.473
In 2009, Sun and colleagues separated itch from pain in mice.

41
00:03:02.773 --> 00:03:07.713
They ablated, or killed off, one set of spinal neurons marked by GRPR.

42
00:03:09.213 --> 00:03:13.813
Scratching to tested itch stimuli dropped sharply, while measured pain behaviours

43
00:03:13.813 --> 00:03:14.813
did not change.

44
00:03:15.783 --> 00:03:21.443
In 2020, Tan and colleagues offered mice sugar against acesulfame K, equally

45
00:03:21.443 --> 00:03:22.603
attractive at first.

46
00:03:23.943 --> 00:03:26.103
Preference shifted within 24 hours.

47
00:03:27.483 --> 00:03:33.103
By 48 hours, mice drank almost only sugar, even mice unable to taste sweetness.

48
00:03:34.443 --> 00:03:38.483
In this assay, learned preference did not require sweet-taste signalling.

49
00:03:38.483 --> 00:03:44.983
Across every test, animal actions become trustworthy evidence only with sharp

50
00:03:44.983 --> 00:03:45.503
controls.
